On Saturday evening, Sabine comes over to my place.
She brings her small dog Bruno with her.
Bruno happily runs into the flat and sniffs everywhere.
"It smells wonderful in here," Sabine says in greeting.
We sit down at the table and I serve the food.
Sabine tries it immediately and smiles.
"This tastes really fantastic, Maya!" she praises.
"Thank you very much," I reply, and I am very happy.
We eat in peace and talk about our week.
Meanwhile, Bruno is sleeping comfortably under the table.
Later, we eat dessert.
We suddenly talk about January.
"Do you remember our first meeting?" I ask.
Sabine laughs out loud.
"Oh yes," she says, "you were freezing so much in the stairwell!"
"And I called you 'Frau Krüger'," I laugh.
We both find that very funny today.
That cold, dark January feels so far away now.
We sit together for a long time and chat.
I am really glad that I have this great friend.
